{"duration_api_ms":124057,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"797f9281-c2cb-4d22-a9c3-548fda9ec49c","total_cost_usd":0.681367,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39982,"cache_read_input_tokens":268295,"output_tokens":15389,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":850},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39982,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":49554,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":15389,"cacheReadInputTokens":268295,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39982,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.681367,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":850,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote 156 tests in `tests/test_agent.py`. 155 pass and 1 fails. The failure is a real bug in the library, and since I wasn't allowed to change the library, I left the test failing rather than weaken it.\n\n**The bug:** `parse.parse()` matches case-sensitively by default when it should ignore case (`parse/__init__.py:947`).\n- Its own docstring says \"The default behaviour is to match strings case insensitively.\"\n- `search`, `findall`, `compile` and `Parser` all default to `case_sensitive=False`.\n- `parse()` alone defaults to `case_sensitive=True`.\n\nSo `parse.parse(\"Hello {}\", \"hello world\")` returns `None`, but `compile(\"Hello {}\").parse(\"hello world\")` matches. The test that catches this is `TestCaseSensitivity::test_parse_default_is_case_insensitive`. Changing that default to `False` should make the whole suite pass.\n\nWhat the tests cover:\n- **Basic matching:** fixed, named, dotted, hyphenated and `[indexed]` field names, repeated names, and `{{ }}` escaping.\n- **Rejecting bad input:** regex special characters in the format are treated as plain text, the whole string must match, and a type mismatch on a repeated name raises an error.\n- **Number types:** `d n b o x X`, including signs, prefixes like `0x`, `,`/`_` digit grouping, width, padding and `=` alignment; also `f F e E g G %` with nan/inf and `.0f`.\n- **Text types and alignment:** `w W s S D l`, width and precision limits, `< > ^` alignment, and fill characters that are special in regex.\n- **Dates and times:** all the `t*` types (with AM/PM and time zones) and strftime-style formats like `%Y-%m-%d`.\n- **Custom types:** `extra_types` and `with_pattern`, including patterns with their own groups, which shifts the position of later fields.\n- **Other features:** `search`/`findall` with `pos`/`endpos`, `evaluate_result=False`, `Match`, match spans, `Result`, the `Parser` text form, pickling, and the `int_convert`/`FixedTzOffset`/`extract_format` helpers.\n\nTwo of my tests failed on the first run because the tests themselves were wrong, and I fixed them. The run also shows one Python `DeprecationWarning` about parsing a date without a year.\n\nTo run: `<repo>/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests`","ttft_ms":2319,"type":"result","duration_ms":126353,"uuid":"37ef4a20-4972-44e3-b715-b2a7ee3cf23a","ttft_stream_ms":1144,"time_to_request_ms":213,"first_content_frame_ms":1144,"queu